Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:53:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] SystemUI: Read the applied retro style from
 Settings.Secure

The RetroStyle app runs as a system app on SELinux-enforcing builds,
where it can't set custom persist.* properties without extra policy.
It writes the resolved style to the secure setting retro_ui_applied
instead (style, variant, anchor, ... as key=value pairs), and SystemUI
reads that once per process through RetroUiApplied.
